{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:63974243617d0761","name":"Storm IV Twin-Pod Cloud Car","source":{"id":"source:reference-63974243617d0761","title":"Storm IV Twin-Pod Cloud Car","revision":20780,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:30:21Z","sha256":"0f2fc7ab7c887522fd1d9281879fc1793063a64fb9dd88bb8b22a155b955d590","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20780","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Storm%20IV%20Twin-Pod%20Cloud%20Car&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-63974243617d0761","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dawn of Defiance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Defiance"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["The Queen of Air and Darkness"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Queen_of_Air_and_Darkness","referenceId":"reference:807bd67869870b44"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Wing Guard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Wing_Guard","referenceId":"reference:d74477954346a060"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["This oddly shaped ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"}," has two pods to each side of a connecting fuselage. Both pods are painted orange, with a cockpit protruding from the top. The Cloud Cars are the same kind that escorted you into ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bespin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bespin","referenceId":"reference:9fbf56e3fbef483c"},", though they are much less friendly now."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Cloud Car is an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"}," that uses both a repulsorlift system and an ion engine, allowing it to operate at near-orbital altitudes and very high speeds. Though Cloud Cars are not ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"},", they can effectively engage in combat with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"}," within a planet's atmosphere. Although their power generators limit them to weaker weapons than those used by typical fighters, in large numbers, Cloud Cars can defend against attacks on cities and ground installations. They can't hold off ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", but they have a good track record against bombers operating below orbital altitudes.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because they don't have to be fully space-capable, Cloud Cars are significantly cheaper than ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},". They are popular with planetary police, paramilitary groups, rangers, and scouts, as well as with bounty hunters who have ships large enough to carry a Cloud Car from planet to planet. The vessels are most common on worlds that have towers many kilometers high (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},") and those that have suspended or floating cities (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bespin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bespin","referenceId":"reference:9fbf56e3fbef483c"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Storm IV Twin-Pod Cloud Car is typical of such vessels, though its double-cockpit arrangement is unusual. Bespin Motors first developed the model as a patrol craft for Cloud City security forces. When the Storm IV proved successful, the company began producing models for export, and others have since designed their own versions of Cloud Cars.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Storm IV Cloud Car is the standard craft used by Bespin's Wing Guard to patrol the skies above the gas giant. These Cloud Cars are extremely fast and maneuverable, though their hulls are weaker than a Starfighter's and their weapons are no match for the superior shielding of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Wing Guard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Wing_Guard","referenceId":"reference:d74477954346a060"}," in these vessels are Imperial loyalists dispatched against the wishes of the Parliament of Guilds. They were informed that the heroes murdered an Imperial officer, and they believe it is their duty to stop the heroes from escaping justice (an act they hope will earn them favor with the Empire).\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Storm IV Twin-Pod Cloud Car Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +6; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 15 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 10), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"